# P18-V01 Remoting nullable ext-fields — 2026-10-17T11:53:46Z

- Repository branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`.
- Java oracle: RocketMQ 5.5.1 commit
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`; Java checkout remained read-only.
- Closed the direct Java `HashMap<String, String>` null-key/null-value gap in
  RemotingCommand. Added public `ExtFields` with nullable lookup, insert,
  remove, and `putIfAbsent` adapters; JSON and RocketMQ binary encoding now
  follow the invoked Java map behavior. The null-key JSON name is the literal
  `"null"`; null values are omitted from JSON and both null-key/null-value
  entries are omitted from RocketMQ binary map encoding.
- Added invoked Java fixture cases for map membership/lookups, display, JSON,
  binary serialization, nullable `addExtField`, and `putIfAbsent` replacing a
  present null value. Migrated public command call sites, tests, examples, and
  benchmark construction to `ExtFields`.
- Removed `DerefMut` from `ExtFields`: exposing the backing `BTreeMap` mutably
  allowed `.entry()` or index mutation to bypass nullable-map invariants. Added
  safe `get_mut` and a regression proving replacement leaves one entry per key.
- Code/test/fixture commit: `c07d3ac2 fix(remoting): preserve nullable
  extension fields`.
